  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainability of services for Key Populations in MENA region - World - Multicountry MENA Key Populations (01-Jan-2019-31-Dec-2021)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multicountry MENA Key Populations, HIV, Frontline AIDS (FA)This program has the following goals: To increase the sustainability of quality HIV prevention, treatment and care services for key populations (KP) in MENA that would accelerate progress on UNAIDS Fast-track targets. The objectives of this program are: Reduction of structural barriers for key populations to access services and be retained in care, as evidenced by stigma index and other surveys..  Increased number of innovative and sustainable service delivery models across the region..  Increased domestic financing for quality HIV prevention, treatment and care services for KPs through public health systems, community systems or through social contracting..  Increased number of CSOs and KP networks with improved institutional capacity to address the needs of KPs and collaborate with health systems to address identified issues..  Increased amount of funding mobilized by CSOs and KP networks from public, private and other sources to better address the needs of KPs..  Increased number of existing CSOs working on broader health and gender issues integrating HIV services in their programs..  Increased number of existing local CSOs and networks registered and having legal status.</narrative>
  </description>
